.SH NAME
cwal \- generate dynamic color schemes from images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cwal
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fB--img\fR \fIimage_path\fR
.br
.B cwal
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fB--random\fR [\fIdirectory\fR]
.br
.B cwal
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fB--theme\fR \fItheme_name|random_dark|random_light|random_all\fR
.br
.B cwal
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fB--restore\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cwal
is a fast and lightweight command-line tool for generating dynamic color
schemes from images.
It extracts dominant colors from an image and applies them to your terminal,
applications, and other system components, providing a cohesive and visually
appealing desktop experience.
.PP
On each run, cwal processes the image with an image processing backend,
derives a 16-color palette, writes it to the cache, renders all templates to
their destinations, reloads affected applications, and finally runs the
post-hook script if one is configured.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " "\fIdark|light\fR
Set theme mode (overrides config).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cols16\-mode " "\fIdarken|lighten\fR
Set the 16-color generation mode (overrides config).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-saturation " "\fIfloat\fR
Set overall saturation (overrides config).
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-contrast " "\fIfloat\fR
Set the contrast ratio (overrides config).
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-alpha " "\fIfloat\fR
Set alpha transparency (0.0-1.0, overrides config).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-out\-dir " "\fIpath\fR
Set the output directory for all generated files (overrides config).
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-backend " "\fIname\fR
Set the image processing backend (overrides config).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-img " "\fIimage_path\fR
Specify the image to process.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-script " "\fIscript_path\fR
Run a script after processing.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-reload
Do not reload applications after processing.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-restore
Re-apply the last used wallpaper.
No image is required; the image path is read from the previous run
(see
.BR cwal (5)).
Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-img ,
.BR \-\-random ,
or
.BR \-\-theme .
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-list\-backends
List all available image processing backends and exit.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-list\-themes
List all available themes and exit.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress all output.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-random " [\fIdirectory\fR]"
Select a random image.
If the directory is omitted, the directory saved in the config
(\fI[random] random_dir\fR, see
.BR cwal (5)) is used.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-theme " "\fItheme_name|random_dark|random_light|random_all\fR
Select a predefined theme, or a random dark, light, or any theme.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-preview
Show the generated palette preview.
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-\-skip\-cursor
Skip writing the cursor color sequence.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version number and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display the help message and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 255
Error (missing arguments, invalid configuration, image processing failure).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for configuration, defaults to
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory for cached output, defaults to
.IR ~/.cache .
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for user data files (templates, themes), defaults to
.IR ~/.local/share .
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_DIRS
Colon-separated list of system data directories searched for system-wide
templates and themes, defaults to
.IR /usr/local/share:/usr/share .
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate colors from an image and apply them:
.nf
cwal --img /path/to/image.jpg
.fi
.PP
Pick a random wallpaper from a directory:
.nf
cwal --random ~/Pictures/wallpapers
.fi
.PP
Pick a random wallpaper using the directory saved in the config:
.nf
cwal --random
.fi
.PP
Apply a predefined theme:
.nf
cwal --theme random_all
.fi
.PP
Re-apply the last used wallpaper:
.nf
cwal --restore
.fi
.PP
Tune the output:
.nf
cwal --img /path/to/image.jpg --alpha 0.8 --saturation 0.1
.fi
